{"id": "section-body-18316", "title": "Management of Oral Conditions during Pregnancy", "chapterId": "chapter-sixteen", "blocks": [{"id": "body-18316", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Management of Oral Conditions during Pregnancy", "runs": [{"text": "Management"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Oral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Conditions"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "during"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Pregnancy"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1126"}}, {"id": "body-18317", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "The oral changes which are seen in pregnancy include gingivitis, gingival hyperplasia, pyogenic granuloma, and salivary changes.", "runs": [{"text": "The"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "oral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "changes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "which"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "seen"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pregnancy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "include"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gingivitis,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gingival"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hyperplasia,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pyogenic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "granuloma,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "salivary "}, {"text": "changes."}]}, {"id": "body-18318", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Gastric acid secretion and the reflux of the acid into the oral cavity leads to worsening of enamel erosion, increased caries risk, increased tooth mobility and loss.", "runs": [{"text": "Gastric"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "acid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "secretion"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "reflux"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "acid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "into"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "oral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cavity"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "leads"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "worsening"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "enamel"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "erosion,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "increased"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "caries"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "risk, increased tooth mobility and loss."}]}, {"id": "body-18320", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "For the first trimester (1-12weeks)", "runs": [{"text": "For"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "first"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "trimester"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(1-"}, {"text": "12weeks)"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-18321", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "During the first trimester, it is recommended that the patients be scheduled to assess their current dental health, to inform them of the changes that they should expect during their pregnancies, and to discuss on how to avoid maternal dental problems that may arise from these changes.", "runs": [{"text": "During"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "first"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "trimester,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "it"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "recommended"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patients"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "scheduled"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "assess"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "their"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "current"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dental"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "health,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inform"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "them of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "changes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "they"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "expect"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "during"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "their"}, {"text": " "}, {